# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `vmr check tsan` (see GateSteps.sanitizerEnvironment).
#
# The Swift concurrency runtime (libswift_Concurrency) is not built with ThreadSanitizer, so the tool cannot see the atomic
# hand-off that orders a continuation's registration against its resume. When a continuation is resumed from another thread
# right after it was registered, it reports a data race in withUnsafe(Throwing)Continuation. The reports seen were in our test
# clock, which resumes parked sleepers under its own lock, and in the async-algorithms package's merge storage.
#
# The patterns are limited to those two frames. A race on our own state elsewhere on the same stack is not what they name.
race:withUnsafeThrowingContinuation
race:withUnsafeContinuation
